atlas carriers

# The protocol grammars this institution actually answers in.
#
# This fact was asserted three times and no two agreed. The /protocols page named
# ten and counted CMS and Web among them, which are surfaces rather than wire
# protocols. The carriers skill said "eighteen" and then listed seventeen.
# capability_fulfillment mapped six coordinates. Nothing was wrong exactly --
# each was describing a different slice -- but there was no answer to "which
# protocols does this institution speak", only three approximations.
#
# The list below was built by probing every candidate. All seventeen answered
# 200. `cmd/BonfyreAtlas/bonfyre-atlas compile-contracts carriers --check` re-probes them, so a
# carrier that stops answering fails rather than staying declared.
#
# Cannot infer: a carrier that answers is not a carrier that is authorized,
# priced, or willing to perform for the caller asking. It answers; that is all
# this contract claims.

carrier_contract served
  carrier x402 /capability
  carrier MPP /mpp/quote
  carrier UCP /ucp/catalog
  carrier ACP /acp/products
  carrier Beckn /beckn/search
  carrier OGC /ogc
  carrier RESO /reso/Property
  carrier MISMO /mismo/subject-property
  carrier ActivityPub /ap/actor
  carrier WebFinger /.well-known/webfinger?resource=acct:bonfyre@aurekai.life
  carrier CloudEvents /events
  carrier WoT /wot/thing
  carrier CAP /cap/alerts
  carrier EPCIS /epcis/events
  carrier OpenRTB /openrtb/bidrequest
  carrier A2A /.well-known/agent.json
  carrier MCP /mcp/resources/
  forbidden_inference a served carrier -> an authorized, priced, or willing one
